tiber264@yahoo.com (evergreen) writes:

> New problem: When I compile NethackW the mail option isn't there.Can
> you compile NethackW with mail?

Just make sure there is #define MAIL in the include/*conf.h file that is
appropriate to your platform, and it is not commented out and not within
some #ifdef block where the condition isn't met.

I see that it is not #defined by default in beconf.h, macconf.h, ntconf.h,
os2conf.h and wceconf.h so you need to add it there if you compile for a
platform using one of those.
And in pcconf.h it is within #ifdef MSDOS, but I don't know whether or not
pcconf.h is used on other than MSDOS versions.

For the other platforms it seems to be #defined by default.
But AFAIK, support for reading your real mail is only implemented in the
unix and VMS versions, on others it just delivers fake mail randomized
from a limited selection that can quickly get annoying.
And MAIL affects bones and save file compatiblility, so changing it will
invalidate existing bones and save files, so if you have a good game
going, finish it before changing the setting.

